WEBVTT

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.080
Welcome back to Chick's Picks
with Chick Hicks.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.480
I'm your host, former and forever,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.480
Piston Cup champion, Chick Hicks.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.440
Doo-doo-doo-doo. This just in...

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.000
Rookie Jackson Storm

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.600
slams the proverbial door
on Lightning McQueen.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.000
(LAUGHS) Oh.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.080
I couldn't have enjoyed it more
if I'd beaten McQueen myself.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.120
Oh, wait, I have. (CHUCKLES)

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.080
But enough about me.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.360
Here to tell you how it happened
is professional number cruncher,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.800
Miss Natalie Certain.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.400
It's a pleasure to be here, Chick.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.640
And actually,
I prefer the term "Statistical Analyst".

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.960
Right. So, who is this
mysterious newcomer, Jackson Storm?

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.680
And why is he so darn fast?

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.360
It's no mystery if you study
the data, Mr. Hicks.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.040
Jackson Storm is part

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.480
of the next generation
of high-tech racers.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.520
Unlike the veterans of yesterday--

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.480
(STAMMERS) What?
Old-timers like this guy? (LAUGHS)

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.320
Um... Right. Storm achieves his top speeds

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.920
by exploiting the numbers.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.160
I refer, of course, to racing data.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.600
Tire pressure, downforce,

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.760
weight distribution, aerodynamics, and...

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.640
next-gens like Storm
are taking advantage.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.000
The racing world is changing.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.880
And for the better if it means my old pal,

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.600
Lightning, is down for the count.
Am I right, Certain?

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.080
Well, if I'm certain of anything, Chick...

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.680
it's that this season is about
to get even more interesting.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.440
CUTLASS: I'll tell you what, Darrell,

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.520
Jackson Storm has
certainly made an impact.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:30.000
We've got six more
next-generation rookies in the field.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.240
DARRELL: With six veterans
fired to clear the way.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.880
Morning, champ.
How's our living legend today?

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.080
Uh... Still very much alive, thank you.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.200
-And I would appreciate--
-You know, I can't believe I get to race

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.880
-the Lightning McQueen.
-(SIGHS)

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.040
In his farewell season.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.160
What are you talking about?

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.920
JACKSON STORM: Oh, green flag.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.680
Good luck out there, champ.
You're gonna need it.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.680
(ENGINE REVVING)

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.760
NATALIE CERTAIN: One reason Storm
and the next-gens are more efficient:

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.120
their ability to hold
the optimum racing line

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.520
every single lap.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.960
CUTLASS: Win number three
for the rookie sensation.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.760
NATALIE CERTAIN:
Storm's in a class of his own.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.720
And a big reason for that: training on
the newest cutting-edge simulators.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.120
These machines create a...

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.080
virtual racing experience so real
racers never even have to go outside.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.240
CUTLASS: Storm's ability
to hold that line

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.000
is like nothing we've ever seen.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.400
DARRELL: Four in a row?
Are you kidding me?

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.560
NATALIE CERTAIN:
2% lower drag coefficient.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:25.720
CUTLASS: Oh, what a finish!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.600
NATALIE CERTAIN:
5% increase downforce.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:31.280
-DARRELL: Lucky number seven.
-1.2% higher top speed.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.160
CUTLASS: Amazing! Nine!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.960
Piston Cup winner, Chick Hicks here

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.520
with the racer taking the circuit...
by storm. Jackson Storm.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.520
Another easy win over old "Ka-chow".
Or should I say, "Caboose"?

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.760
Because he's always in the back.
Am I right?

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.800
No, no, no, Chick.
McQueen is a crafty veteran champ.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.160
He's the elder statesman of the sport.
You know?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.760
Takes everything I got to beat him.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.600
(SIGHS) You got to be kidding me.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.080
(REPORTERS CLAMORING)

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.680
REPORTER 1: What changes
are you gonna make

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.920
to get McQueen back on top?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.440
REPORTER 2: Will McQueen try
new training methods?

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.520
REPORTER 3: Is he prepared to retire?

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.720
Come on, guys. Let's not overreact.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:06.880
It's just a slump.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.400
We'll get 'em next week.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.600
Okay, that's enough. No comment.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.160
Not even about Weathers retiring?

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.280
Wait. What?

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.480
Cal Weathers.
He's hanging up his Lightyears.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.840
No. No comment on that either.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:20.880
REPORTER 3: Wait a minute.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:21.960
Please, come on.
You got to give us something.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.040
Hey, Cal! Hey.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.640
Retirement? What's going on?

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.440
(SIGHS)

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.680
You know, I asked my uncle once

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.240
how I'd know when it was time to stop.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.320
You know what he said?

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.960
The youngsters will tell you.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.000
We had some good times together.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.160
I'm gonna miss that the most I think.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.040
Yeah.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.480
NATALIE CERTAIN:
More changes ahead, Chick.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.680
Every week we've seen
veteran racers either retire...

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.400
like Cal Weathers tonight,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.640
or fired to make room
for these younger...

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.000
faster racers.
And, it's not over yet.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.200
ANNOUNCER: Hello racing fans.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.760
Welcome to the Los Angeles 500.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.400
The final race of the Piston Cup season.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.400
It's been a year of surprises--

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.320
BRICK: They can't do this.
I've raced for you guys almost 10 years.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.640
Sorry, Brick. My mind's made up.
I'm giving your number to someone new.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.320
Hey, I had two wins last year!

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.920
SPONSOR: The whole sport's changing.
I'm just doing what I got to do.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.280
Hey, do you know what's
happening with Brick-- Oh!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.840
Wait, you're not Bobby.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.000
(ENGINE REVS)

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.680
The name's Danny, bro.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.440
Hey, champ,
where'd all your friends go?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.320
CUTLASS: A final check of his tires
as Storm settles into the pole position.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.280
DARRELL: Boogity, boogity, boogity.
Let's end this season with a great race.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.200
(ENGINES REVVING)

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.360
That's it, buddy!

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.640
NATALIE CERTAIN: Forty laps to go
and race leader, Jackson Storm...

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.840
is making his way onto pit road
with McQueen on his tail.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.720
A good stop here could mean the
difference between victory and defeat.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.600
Come on, come on. Come on!
Faster, Guido, come on.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.680
I got to get back out there
before he does.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.000
-Guido, hurry up!
-(WHIRRING)

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.200
-(GUIDO SPEAKING ITALIAN)
-(TIRES SQUEALING)

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.160
DARRELL: What a pit stop
by McQueen!

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.720
Man, he just got the lead!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.520
CUTLASS: But can he hold on to it?

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.360
-(PANTING)
-Hey, McQueen, are you all right?

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.840
Listen, don't you worry, pal.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.880
You had a good run.
Enjoy your retirement!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.600
CUTLASS: Storm takes back the lead!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.240
DARRELL: Unbelievable!
McQueen is fading!

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.040
McQueen is fading! Fading fast!

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.360
No. No! No! No!

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.880
No!

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.040
(McQUEEN PANTING)

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:33.640
(GRUNTING)

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.520
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.360
(GASPS)

